### Examples for the VS Code REST Client or IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Local mode has no SSO, so you say who you are with the X-User header.
@gw = http://localhost:8080

### Who am I
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/me
X-User: app_engg_member_1

### Catalogues I am allowed to see (OPA decides)
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/catalogues
X-User: app_engg_member_1

### One catalogue with its capability cards and options
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/catalogues/app_engg_catalogue
X-User: app_engg_member_1

### Service details tab: services provided and tools and resources
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/catalogues/app_engg_catalogue/service-details
X-User: app_engg_member_1

### Raise a request. Backup owner is mandatory.
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/requests
X-User: app_engg_member_1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "catalogueId": "app_engg_catalogue",
  "capability": "Grant repository access",
  "option": "Read access",
  "justification": "Need to review the payments repository",
  "backupOwner": "app_engg_member_2",
  "permanent": false,
  "months": 1,
  "days": 0
}

### My requests
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/requests?scope=mine
X-User: app_engg_member_1

### Requests waiting for the L1 approver
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/requests?scope=approvals
X-User: sol_engg_lead

### Full detail of one request
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/requests/REQ-1001
X-User: sol_engg_lead

### Approve (L1)
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/requests/REQ-1001/decision
X-User: sol_engg_lead
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "APPROVED", "comment": "Fine for one month" }

### Approve (L2). After this the request becomes ACTIVE.
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/requests/REQ-1001/decision
X-User: manpreet
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "APPROVED" }

### Activity of one request
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/requests/REQ-1001/activity
X-User: sol_engg_lead

### Delegate a waiting step
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/requests/REQ-1001/delegate
X-User: sol_engg_lead
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "app_engg_member_2" }

### Audit log and its integrity check
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/audit
X-User: super_admin_1

###
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/audit/verify
X-User: super_admin_1

### Change who can see a catalogue. This is an OPA change request.
### It needs the same two approvals. When approved, provisioning publishes it to OPA.
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/requests
X-User: sol_engg_lead
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "catalogueId": "app_engg_catalogue",
  "capability": "Grant repository access",
  "option": "Read access",
  "justification": "Let Sol Engg see the Product catalogue",
  "backupOwner": "manpreet",
  "permanent": true,
  "opaPath": "catalogs/app_engg_catalogue",
  "opaValue": { "team": "app_engg", "creator": "sol_engg_lead", "visible_to": ["App Engg", "Sol Engg"] }
}
